add("Task 4, the emitter changes that alter emitted code: (a) SHL, SHR and SAR of a literal value by a non-literal count now load the result from a 96-byte read-only window (shift_literal_by_non_literal, emitter.cpp:5254-5326 at v0.16.7); (b) end-of-block stack writes are ordered by stack index instead of an unordered_map keyed by heap address, and words that came from general registers are rebuilt with vmovq and vpinsrq (emitter.cpp:1453-1652, mov_words_to_ymm at :2060-2071); (c) a memory bounds check is skipped when the same offset element was already checked for at least the same size (emitter.cpp:6301-6312); (d) MSTORE8 from a stack slot loads four bytes and stores the low byte (emitter.cpp:3399-3412); (e) a block whose stack range exceeds 1,024 jumps to the error label (emitter.cpp:1342); (f) CLZ is branchless. Read line by line.",
    "Each is sound as read. (a) The count is first clamped to 256 by destructive_mov_stack_elem_to_bounded_rax (emitter.cpp:4122-4190, unchanged), k = count/8 selects a byte offset into the value placed next to 32 bytes of zero fill (SHL below it, SHR and SAR above it, the fill all ones for a negative SAR literal), b = count mod 8 shifts each lane and a second load one byte further supplies the b carried bits, which for SAR come from the fill and give the sign; for count 256 both loads read only fill; rax is outside the three register groups (emitter.cpp:639), so the base register cannot overwrite the count. (b) The order of the writes changes, the dependency counting and cycle resolution do not; the temporary register is taken while free and no allocation happens before its last use. (c) Memory never shrinks inside a frame, so a passed check stays passed, and the gas for that size has been paid. (d) and (f) give the same byte and count. (e) No stack size can pass both bounds of such a block. A test contract with 27 literals (among them the PoolManager's own: 1, 2^256-1, 0x8421084210842108cc6318c6db6d54be of BitMath.sol:22, 0x8040...7077 of BitMath.sol:40-42, 0xffffffff<<224) and 312 counts (0 to 300, 511, 512, 2^64, 2^128, 2^255, 2^256-1 and others), with the count from CALLDATALOAD, through AND and through MLOAD, compiles 231 of its 243 shifts through the new path at v0.16.7; all 151,632 words per tag equal Python integers on both engines at both tags (seed 2727).",
    f"{GH7}category/vm/compiler/ir/x86/emitter.cpp ; {W}/out/tagdiff/category_vm_compiler_ir_x86_emitter.cpp.diff ; {W}/out/shift/summary.json ; {W}/scripts/shiftlit.py ; src/libraries/BitMath.sol:22 ; src/libraries/BitMath.sol:40-42 ; src/libraries/TickBitmap.sol:73 ; src/libraries/TickBitmap.sol:97 ; src/libraries/TickBitmap.sol:110")
